\par\par \b \uc2 Why \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Is Investing Another $13 Billion in India's AI Data Centers -- Barrons.com\b0\par\par\uc2 By Mackenzie Tatananni \par \uc2 336 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 15:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has committed an additional $13 billion to expand its \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cloud infrastructure in India as it doubles down on the world's most populous country.\par \par \uc2 This latest infusion brings \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's total planned investment in India to $48 billion between 2026 and 2030. The fresh capital will be used specifically to expand data center capacity in Mumbai and Hyderabad, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 India has become the next frontier for hyperscalers, or tech giants building massive data centers to house cloud computing infrastructure. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  pledged to invest $35 billion in the country last year, around the same time \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  earmarked $17.5 billion of its own.\par \par \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 -owned \uc2 Google\uc2 , another premier hyperscaler, announced in October that it would spend $15 billion over a five-year span to expand data-center capacity in southern India.\par \par \uc2 As for \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , the e-commerce giant plans to be "a long-term partner in India's growth story," CEO \uc2 Andy Jassy\uc2  said in a statement Thursday. The announcement coincided with Jassy's visit to New Delhi, where he met with Prime Minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's foothold in India goes back more than a decade. The company first entered the market with the launch of a price comparison site called Junglee in 2012, followed by a dedicated online shopping marketplace in 2013.\par \par \uc2 Its AI ambitions in the country, however, have gathered pace over the past few years, in line with an explosion of demand for the technology. As \uc2 Amazon Web Services\uc2  expanded its footprint in India, it began selling cloud-based AI and machine learning tools to local enterprises and government entities.\par \par \uc2 Write to Mackenzie Tatananni at mackenzie.tatananni@barrons.com\par \par \uc2 This content was created by Barron's, which is operated by Dow Jones & Co. Barron's is published independently from Dow Jones Newswires and The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 25, 2026 09:18 ET (13:18 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260625em6p0023t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
