\par\par \b \uc2 Micron Is the New \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 , It Just Changed the AI Game -- Barrons.com\b0\par\par\uc2 1,874 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 14:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Move over \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 , there's a new chip champion in town. Memory-chip maker \uc2 Micron Technology\uc2  has taken its title as the primary beneficiary of the huge wave of spending on \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  infrastructure. Now the question is whether it can keep it.\par \par \uc2 Micron's earnings figures were just as mind-blowing as \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 's most impressive quarters. Managing to quadruple revenue with gross margins of 85% is a rare feat. And Micron insists it's not a one-off, with the memory-chip shortage set to last at least another 18 months.\par \par \uc2 Where once commentators spoke of an "\uc2 Nvidia\uc2  tax," it has been replaced for large tech companies such as Apple with a "Micron tax" -- or at least a memory toll, as Micron's South Korean rivals are reaping similar rewards. U.S. investors wanting to spread their bets on the memory boom will soon have the option of also investing in \uc2 SK Hynix\uc2  as it plans to list American depositary receipts next month.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  also provides a cautionary tale for Micron shareholders. While still the leading AI chip supplier, \uc2 Nvidia\uc2 's stock has been an underperformer this year. A flood of new AI processors is disrupting what had once been a quasi-monopoly and the competition shows no signs of slowing -- just this week ChatGPT-developer \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  unveiled its custom AI chip designed with \uc2 Broadcom\uc2 , while \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  announced supply deals with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Will Big Tech also seek to undermine Micron and its South Korean peers? Micron is taking pre-emptive action by locking in long-term supply deals with fixed price ranges, hoping to keep its big customers on side. But companies such as \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Google\uc2 -parent \uc2 Alphabet\uc2  are under stock market pressure to show they can control their AI spending, which means at the very least they will be investigating ways to reduce the amount they are paying to Micron.\par \par \uc2 Micron has taken the AI stock crown. But as \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  has found, being on top makes you a target.\par \par \uc2 -- Adam Clark\par \par \uc2 Get more of the journalism you love. Choose Barron's as a preferred source in \uc2 Google\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Micron Smashes Expectations. The Chip Shortage Continues.\par \par \uc2 Micron Technology\uc2  revenue quadrupled in the second quarter, and the chip maker said the demand-driven chip shortage will last beyond 2027, a year after previous guidance that the shortage would end early next year. Micron has 16 long-term deals to supply chips. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- The stock surged more than 15% in after-hours trading after the company \par       beat Wall Street's expectations. Micron reported adjusted earnings of \par       $25.11 a share and revenue of $41.5 billion, up 346% from a year ago. \par       Adjusted gross margin was 85%, and adjusted operating margin was 81%. \par  \par    -- Sales growth in the recent quarter was led by the company's two \par       data-center segments which combined for 415% growth from last year to $25 \par       billion. They now account for 61% of total sales. Micron and its peers \par       have gone from a cyclical, commodity-like business to the hottest part of \par       the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 artificial intelligence\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trade. \par  \par    -- The data-center investment boom has driven prices for memory and storage \par       chips into the stratosphere. Guidance was similarly strong. Fiscal \par       fourth-quarter revenue is expected to be $49 billion to $51 billion with \par       adjusted earnings of $31 a share at the midpoint, also well above \par       expectations. \par  \par    -- Micron had $18 billion in free cash flow in the quarter, and at the end \par       of May had $26 billion in cash, equivalents, and short term investments, \par       up from $14 billion three months ago. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's Next: Ultimately, this historic upcycle may face a painful end. But Micron is using its current market power to push customers into five-year supply agreements. The deals include cash deposits, pricing ranges, and minimum purchases.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Adam Levine and Liz Moyer\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qualcomm\f28 \uc2 \f2  Hikes Sales Target, Reveals Meta as Data-Center Customer\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It wasn't just Micron that signaled the AI boom was alive and well on Wednesday. Chip maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Qualcomm\f28 \uc2 \f2  treated investors to a flurry of important updates about its data-center business, including the reveal that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Meta Platforms\f28 \uc2 \f2  is among its customers. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Qualcomm\f28 \uc2 \f2  revealed at an investor day that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Facebook\f28 \uc2 \f2  parent \f28 \uc2 \f2 Meta\f28 \uc2 \f2  would use \par       its Dragonfly C1000 central processing units when they become available \par       in 2028. "We're excited to continue partnering with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Qualcomm Technologies\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par       as they design the next generation of CPUs for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Meta\f28 \uc2 \f2 ," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Meta\f28 \uc2 \f2  CEO \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mark \par       Zuckerberg\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. \par  \par    -- Just hours later, the company raised its fiscal 2029 non-handset revenue \par       target to $40 billion, almost double its previous guidance. The company \par       also expects $15 billion of data-center sales by that point. \par  \par    -- IT giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Microsoft\f28 \uc2 \f2  will use another of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Qualcomm\f28 \uc2 \f2 's new products -- the \par       company's High Bandwidth Compute chip architecture, which is expected in \par       mid-2027. \par  \par    -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Qualcomm\f28 \uc2 \f2 's push into data centers comes as it seeks to diversify away \par       from the smartphones, tablets, and gaming devices powered by its chips. \par       Qualcomm expects handsets to make up just one-third of its revenue by \par       fiscal 2029, down from 72% in fiscal 2025. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's Next: Chip stocks have struggled in recent days due to worries about how long so-called hyperscalers -- including Meta and Microsoft -- can maintain their aggressive data-center spending. But the slew of announcements, coupled with Micron's strong results, could help revive faith in the AI trade.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- George Glover\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Big Bank Stress Test Results Are Out. This Year's Twist.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The largest U.S. banks have enough capital to continue lending to households and businesses through even the most treacherous economic conditions, according to the Federal Reserve's annual stress test. The results don't immediately affect bank capital levels, though some are already announcing capital plans. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- The 32 banks subjected to a series of hypothetical adverse scenarios \par       featuring, at worst, a 10% unemployment rate, double-digit real estate \par       price declines, and plunging stocks can absorb $708 billion in loan \par       losses and still function as lenders. \par  \par    -- The results should instill confidence in the financial system. Regulators \par       introduced the annual stress tests after the 2008-09 financial crisis as \par       a way to gauge banks' health and expose potential risk areas. But the \par       Trump administration wants to pull back on bank regulation and is \par       rewiring the test process. \par  \par    -- The Fed is waiting until 2027 to calculate a key piece of how much \par       capital banks must hold. Banks often announce new buyback and dividend \par       plans after the results come out. This year, those plans will be based on \par       2025 stress capital buffers, or the capital lenders must hold above \par       requirements. \par  \par    -- JPMorgan announced plans to raise its quarterly dividend 10% and buy back \par       another $50 billion of shares. Wells Fargo and Goldman Sachs said they \par       were raising their dividends by 11% each, while Morgan Stanley is raising \par       its dividend to $1.15 a share and buying back another $20 billion of \par       shares. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's Next: The Fed has opted to freeze those levels until it can incorporate input from banks into next year's stress test models. Regulators appointed by President Donald Trump are working to overhaul the way they run stress tests after years of pressure by bank lobbyists.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Rebecca Ungarino\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trump Cancels Housing Bill Signing. What Happens Next.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Donald Trump's abrupt signing ceremony cancellation has tossed his housing affordability push into chaos just months before the midterm elections -- and ruffled a lot of feathers on Capitol Hill. Trump is demanding lawmakers pass a stalled bill with strict voter eligibility limits before he'll sign the housing bill. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- The bipartisan 21st Century Road to Housing Act he was supposed to sign \par       Wednesday includes provisions that will encourage new-home construction \par       and ease rules around financing manufactured homes, and other provisions. \par       It also bans institutional investors from purchasing more existing family \par       homes. \par  \par    -- House Speaker Mike Johnson indicated the delay may not last. He said he \par       assured the president he would attach aspects of the voter eligibility \par       bill to another potential bill to pass later this year. The president has \par       10 days to sign or veto the housing bill. \par  \par    -- Stephen Kim, an Evercore analyst who covers home builders, said they \par       believe the housing bill will still become law. Even if the president \par       vetoed the bill, "Congress has enough votes to override," Kim wrote, \par       citing Evercore strategist Matt Aks. \par  \par    -- It was supported by the National Association of Home Builders, whose \par       Chairman Bill Owens said before the cancellation that it was expected to \par       help increase the nation's housing supply by reducing regulatory barriers \par       and encouraging local governments to reform zoning and land-use policies, \par       easing the affordability crisis. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's Next: The voter eligibility rules face a high hurdle. Senate Republicans have a 53-47 majority, but the bill requires 60 votes to advance because of the filibuster rule. No Democrats support the bill. Senate Majority Leader John Thune has rejected Trump's calls to eliminate the filibuster rule.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Joe Light and Liz Moyer\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wendy's Stock Soars. The Meme Warriors Are At It Again.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 25 Jun 2026 08:16 ET \par Micron Is the New Nvidia, It Just Changed the AI -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reddit's meme stock warriors appear to be at it again, taking to their WallStreetBets subreddit to urge people to buy shares in the struggling fast-food chain Wendy's. That forced the stock up 35% and made it more actively traded than some red-hot tech shares like Micron Technology and Intel. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Why was the burger chain known for its square patties and Frosty frozen \par       desserts the target? In news, Wendy's named former Potbelly Sandwich \par       Works CFO Steve Cirulis as CFO and Chief Strategy Officer this week. CEO \par       Robert Wright has a turnaround plan under way. \par  \par    -- WallStreetBets users in the past have used the forum to talk up so-called \par       meme stocks like GameStop and AMC Entertainment. And Wendy's has received \par       love from retail investors before, enjoying a brief surge in the summer \par       2021. The stock has slumped 47% over the past year. \par  \par    -- Wendy's looks well-positioned for a short squeeze, when a stock suddenly \par       jumps, forcing short sellers to buy back shares to cover their losing \par       bets. Those purchases in turn drive a stock's price even higher. Short \par       interest was about 30% of Wendy's public float on Wednesday. \par  \par    -- Activist Nelson Peltz's Trian Fund Management is a longtime investor, \par       with 14,943,000 shares, or about $93 million as of Tuesday's close. \par       Wendy's market value, at just $1.2 billion as of Tuesday, is far smaller \par       than rival McDonald's, making stock easier to move with concentrated \par       buying. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 What's Next: Meme-stock rallies tend to feed on momentum. Once unusual trading activity begins attracting attention on social media, the story can become self-reinforcing as more traders pile in. Investors will also watch whether the speculative rally could actually help Wendy's underlying business going forward.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- George Glover and Evie Liu\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Newsletter edited by Liz Moyer, Patrick O'Donnell, Callum Keown\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This content was created by Barron's, which is operated by Dow Jones & Co. Barron's is published independently from Dow Jones Newswires and The Wall Street Journal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 25, 2026 08:16 ET (12:16 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260625em6p001t5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
