\par\par \b \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  Stock Gains Even as AI Chip Competition Hots Up -- Barrons.com\b0\par\par\uc2 By Adam Clark \par \uc2 282 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 12:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  was rising early Thursday. The chip maker was benefiting from widespread semiconductor cheer, even as more options came onto the \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  processor market.\par \par \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  shares were up 1.5% at $201.94 in premarket trading with chip stocks generally gaining after \uc2 Micron Technology\uc2 's blowout earnings. The stock closed down 0.5% at $199 the previous day.\par \par \uc2 As Barron's has written, \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  looks to be establishing a trading range with a floor of roughly $200, after breaking through that level in April. A relatively cheap valuation and increasing dividend and share buybacks could support the stock.\par \par \uc2 However, the prospect of a resumed rally might be hampered by increasing competition in the AI chip market. Just this week ChatGPT-developer \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  has unveiled its custom AI chip designed with \uc2 Broadcom\uc2 , while \uc2 Qualcomm\uc2  announced supply deals with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Such deals don't necessarily mean \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  is losing any business -- its graphics-processing units are still the superior option for many AI workloads and many big technology companies have already committed to using its next-generation Vera Rubin hardware. But investors are likely to remain cautious until they see evidence of whether \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  can maintain its market share.\par \par \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  was a Barron's stock pick in mid-May when shares were trading at $226.\par \par \uc2 Write to Adam Clark at adam.clark@barrons.com\par \par \uc2 This content was created by Barron's, which is operated by Dow Jones & Co. Barron's is published independently from Dow Jones Newswires and The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 25, 2026 06:15 ET (10:15 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260625em6p00157\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
