\par\par \b \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to Invest Additional $13 Billion in India by 2030 -- Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kimberley Kao \par \uc2 360 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 12:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  plans to spend an additional $13 billion in India by 2030 to expand and support \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial-intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cloud infrastructure in the country.\par \par \uc2 The planned outlay builds on the $35 billion investment across its businesses in India that was outlined in December, the U.S. tech company said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The latest investment will go toward expanding \uc2 Amazon Web Services\uc2 ' data-center capacity in Mumbai and Hyderabad, as well as giving startups, enterprises and government organizations access to custom AI chips, managed AI services, cloud technologies and developer tools, it said.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  also plans to launch more than 20 fulfillment centers and over 100 delivery stations across India this year, it said.\par \par \uc2 "As we grow \uc2 Amazon\uc2  in India, our business priorities align with India's priorities of democratizing access to AI, digitizing small businesses, creating jobs, and enabling exports," \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Andy Jassy\uc2  said during his visit to New Delhi, where he met Indian Prime Minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company has committed to supporting 3.8 million jobs in India and $80 billion in cumulative exports.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has earmarked more than $88 billion for investments in India from 2010 to 2030.\par \par \uc2 India has drawn tens of billions of dollars from major technology companies this year, underlining its appeal as an AI and cloud hub.\par \par \uc2 Large U.S. data-center firms--also known as hyperscalers--are drawn to the country as its 1.4 billion consumers are some of the most prolific users of data and AI chatbots.\par \par \uc2 In October, \uc2 Google\uc2  announced a $15 billion investment in data centers in southeastern India, as well as undersea-cable links. In December, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  unveiled its largest-ever investment in Asia, with a $17.5 billion pledge to develop the country's cloud and AI infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, India introduced a policy to attract more tech investments. The government is giving global hyperscalers that use India-based data centers for global operations long-term tax breaks.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kimberley Kao at kimberley.kao@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 25, 2026 06:20 ET (10:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260625em6p00163\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
