\par\par \b \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2  Sees New AI Opportunities as Embedded-Software Business Accelerates\b0\par\par\uc2 By Adriano Marchese \par \uc2 519 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 13:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2  lifted its fiscal 2027 outlook on higher first-quarter results, driven by embedded-software growth and expanding opportunities with \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2 , whose name was once synonymous with the early smartphone era, sees growing opportunities in its general embedded management platform, which helps run AI-enabled industrial and robotic systems as companies look to bring AI into machinery.\par \par \uc2 Investors have increasingly focused on the technology's potential as a new growth avenue beyond \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2 's core automotive software business, a trend that has helped drive the stock to more than double since the start of the year.\par \par \uc2 GEM builds on the same real-time operating system technology that underpins \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2 's QNX software, which is widely used in automobiles and other safety-critical systems. Chief Executive \uc2 John Giamatteo\uc2  said the company sees multi-year growth opportunities ahead, particularly in software-defined vehicles and the broader embedded systems market.\par \par \uc2 "We believe these opportunities significantly enhance \uc2 QNX\uc2 's long-term potential," Giamatteo said.\par \par \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2  now sees fiscal 2027 revenue of $594 million to $621 million, higher than its previous forecast of $584 million to $611 million.\par \par \uc2 The increase comes partly from higher QNX revenue targets, now at $295 million to $312 million, up from $290 million to $307 million previously, but still in line with analyst guidance of $301.1 million, according to FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Secure Communications expectations remain unchanged, while licensing revenue is expected to be slightly higher.\par \par \uc2 Adjusted earnings are seen at 16 to 20 cents a share in fiscal 2027. Wall Street projects adjusted earnings of 18 cents a share.\par \par \uc2 For the quarter ended May 31, \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2  posted net income of $8.5 million, or 1 cent a share, up from $1.9 million, or zero a share, in the comparable quarter a year ago.\par \par \uc2 On an adjusted basis, which strips out exceptional items and one-off costs, earnings came to 4 cents a share, ahead of both its own guidance range of 2 cents to 3 cents, and analyst expectations of 3 cents a share, according to FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Revenue rose 26% to $152.9 million, topping its own guidance range of $132 million to $140 million and analyst expectations of $137.2 million.\par \par \uc2 The double-digit revenue jump was fueled by strong expansions across both QNX, which grew 26% to $72.3 million, and its Secure Communications segment, which rose 24% to $73.6 million.\par \par \uc2 Looking ahead to \uc2 BlackBerry\uc2 's second quarter, revenue guidance is pegged at $137 million to $148 million, up from $129.6 million, with analyst forecasts expecting growth to $139.4 million.\par \par \uc2 QNX\uc2  revenue is expected to contribute between $70 million and $75 million, while Secure Communications is guided to be between $57 million and $63 million. Licensing revenue is expected to be about $10 million.\par \par \uc2 Adjusted Ebitda is expected between $20 million and $30 million, and adjusted earnings are seen at 3 to 4 cents a share.\par \par \uc2 Write to Adriano Marchese at adriano.marchese@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 25, 2026 07:17 ET (11:17 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Document DJDN000020260625em6p001hg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
