\par\par \b \uc2 Press Release: \uc2 VCI Global\uc2  Strengthens Capital Alignment Following Premium Warrant Conversion by Institutional Investor\b0\par\par\uc2 830 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 June 2026\par 13:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2026, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR, Malaysia, June 25, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- \uc2 VCI Global Limited\uc2  (NASDAQ: VCIG) ("\uc2 VCI Global\uc2 "), an emerging AI-native operating platform leveraging \b \highlight22\uc2 artificial intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2 , data, governance frameworks, and strategic capital allocation capabilities, today announced a strategic strengthening of its equity capital structure following an institutional commitment from Esousa Group Holdings LLC ("Esousa Holdings"), a New York-based family office.\par \par \uc2 Pursuant to a finalized agreement, Esousa Holdings has elected to convert existing warrants into 880,000 shares of the Company's common stock at a conversion price of US$5.62 per share.\par \par \uc2 Notably, the conversion price represents a 24.9% premium to \uc2 VCI Global\uc2 's closing market price of US$4.50 on June 24, 2026, reflecting institutional confidence in the Company's strategic transformation, long-term growth direction, and continued execution of its AI-native operating platform vision.\par \par \uc2 The institutional decision to convert warrants into equity further demonstrates confidence in \uc2 VCI Global\uc2 's strategic direction, strengthens shareholder alignment, and simplifies the Company's capital structure.\par \par \uc2 "We are very pleased with this strong demonstration of confidence from Esousa Holdings," said Ang Zhi Feng, Chief Financial Officer of \uc2 VCI Global\uc2 . "Their decision to convert these instruments into equity at a premium to the prevailing market price underscores their conviction in our strategic roadmap, commercial pipeline, and continued execution. This transaction represents meaningful alignment between our institutional stakeholders and the Company's long-term vision."\par \par \uc2 The shares issued in connection with this transaction were finalised following completion of the necessary structural and formal reviews. The transaction details will be disclosed in the Company's Report of Foreign Private Issuer on Form 6-K, to be furnished to the \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC).\par \par \uc2 This transaction reinforces \uc2 VCI Global\uc2 's commitment to building a stronger capital foundation as the Company continues to advance its AI-native platform strategy, focusing on intelligent systems, data-driven decision-making, governance infrastructure, and strategic growth initiatives.\par \par \uc2 About \uc2 VCI Global Limited\par \par \uc2 VCI Global Limited\uc2  (NASDAQ: VCIG) is an AI-native operating platform designed to scale and optimize businesses through centralized intelligence, data, and capital discipline.\par \par \uc2 The Company operates a platform-based model in which subsidiaries, affiliates, and portfolio companies plug into \uc2 VCI Global\uc2 's centralized AI, data, governance, and capital allocation systems, enabling faster execution, improved capital efficiency, and scalable growth across multiple industries.\par \par \uc2 VCI Global\uc2 's platform centralizes AI-enabled execution, standardized KPI frameworks, financial and governance controls, and strategic capital allocation, while operating businesses focus on revenue generation, customer relationships, and local execution.\par \par \uc2 The Company maintains exposure across advisory, AI, and digital infrastructure, digital assets, energy, automotive, and consumer sectors, and continuously evaluates opportunities to scale, spin off, divest, or discontinue businesses based on performance, scalability, and return on capital.\par \par \uc2 VCI Global\uc2 's platform-centric approach is designed to enhance productivity, im